PegResponsiveExponentialIrm::updateInterestRateView(uint256,uint256)
├── given market is not set
│   ├── it should revert with IrmMarketNotSet
│   ├── it should not read the oracle
│   └── it should leave state unchanged and emit no events
└── given market is set
    ├── when block.timestamp is less than lastUpdate
    │   ├── it should revert with arithmetic-underflow panic 0x11
    │   └── it should leave state unchanged and emit no events
    ├── when the compound-interest dependency or final fixed-point multiplication overflows for unsupported extreme inputs
    │   ├── it should bubble arithmetic-overflow panic 0x11
    │   └── it should leave state unchanged and emit no events
    └── when elapsed-time and arithmetic inputs are supported
        ├── when elapsed time is zero
        │   └── it should return zero interest and the stored borrowRate
        ├── when totalBorrowed is zero
        │   └── it should return zero interest and the stored borrowRate for any supported elapsed time
        ├── when totalBorrowed and elapsed time are non-zero
        │   ├── it should calculate interest from the stored borrowRate over block.timestamp minus lastUpdate
        │   ├── it should round the final fixed-point debt multiplication down
        │   └── it should return the exact FixedPointMath compound-interest result and the stored borrowRate
        ├── when totalSupply varies while debt, rate and elapsed time remain equal
        │   └── it should return identical values because totalSupply is unused
        ├── it should be callable by any address without market authorization
        ├── it should return the old stored rate without deriving a price-responsive rate
        ├── it should not call the oracle or the bound market
        └── it should leave the complete IRState unchanged and emit no events
